# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vlax-boolean-properties-return-t -- COM boolean properties return T / nil, not :vlax-true / :vlax-false
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-04

* Observed

cador's mock object model stores boolean properties as CL T / NIL:
Application.Visible, Document.Saved, Document.ReadOnly, Block.IsLayout /
IsXRef / IsDynamicBlock / Explodable, ... so (vla-get-visible app) returns T.
ActiveX returns VARIANT_TRUE / VARIANT_FALSE, which Visual LISP presents as
:VLAX-TRUE / :VLAX-FALSE (BricsCAD V26: Document.Active -> :VLAX-TRUE,
probe-triage2). Code written for the vendors compares with :vlax-true
(EPUREE: (= (vla-get-Active dwg) :vlax-true)) and therefore fails on every
property but Document.Active.

Until 2.2.179 :VLAX-TRUE / :VLAX-FALSE were not even defined (they read as
nil, so the comparison happened to hold for T vs nil only by accident of
nil). They are now predefined self-valued symbols, and Document.Active
returns them (com-application-object-properties).

* To do

Probe a few boolean properties on BricsCAD (Application.Visible,
Document.Saved, Block.IsLayout, Layer.LayerOn, Entity.Visible) and the put
side (does vla-put-visible accept T / nil as well as :vlax-true?); then
return :vlax-true / :vlax-false from every boolean property (one place:
the property value conversion), accepting both on put.

* Measured and done (2026-10-05, clautolisp 2.2.183)

probe-triage3 (BricsCAD V26 macOS job 16931597044, V25 Windows job
16931597047; AutoCAD's accoreconsole has no COM):
  - vla-get-* / vlax-get-property of Visible, Saved, ReadOnly, IsLayout,
    IsXRef, LayerOn, Freeze, Lock, Plottable, an entity's Visible:
    :VLAX-TRUE / :VLAX-FALSE on both;
  - vlax-get of a Boolean: the integer -1 / 0;
  - put: :vlax-false, T, nil accepted on both; 0 / -1 accepted by V25
    Windows, refused (E_INVALIDARG) by V26 macOS.
Implemented in cador: *com-boolean-properties*, one conversion on get and
one on put (host-vlax-get-property / -put-property), vlax-get's plain value
-1 / 0, Layer LayerOn / Freeze / Lock / Plottable and entity Visible (they
were missing), the integers refused under a macOS dialect.
vlax-write-enabled-p reads ReadOnly through the new symbols.
Noted, not done: AutoCAD prints the two symbols in lower case
(":vlax-true", probe-triage3 job 16931597043), BricsCAD in upper case.
